/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:1:# Combo variant of 28a6681f (index 39)
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:8:#    - Source task: a 10x10 board shows both the unstable source water and the bottom basin system,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:9:#      and the output keeps that full frame after water settles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:12:#      bottom-anchored basin structure. That crop keeps the basin walls and the water inside them,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:15:#      * columns 3, 7, 11 form three basin walls with heights 6, 4, 6, so the crop later spans
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:17:#      * a supported 3x4 water block sits on a shelf near the top-left, with one leak at column 4;
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:20:#      * under the fused family, the same water must still be simulated on the full board first, but
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:21:#        the visible answer is just the compact lower basin rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:24:#      basins. That keeps the water law recognizable.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:26:#      basin count, basin widths, wall heights, and source water volume. This is enough variation to
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:31:#    - The original upper-guide validation scanned `g[:7]` and inferred guide identity from colors
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:34:#      also appear in the basin. The fused solver therefore removes that parsing block entirely.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:35:#    - The actual settle loop only depends on occupancy (`bg` vs water vs solid), so its straight
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:37:#    - New assumption introduced by cropping: every final water pixel must lie inside the basin crop,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:38:#      otherwise cropping would silently discard water. The generator guarantees this by placing all
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:39:#      source water on a one-leak shelf that fully drains into the lower basin system.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:44:#      separation, so the source structure never merges with the bottom-anchored basin component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:45:#    - Source water is always a side-packed rectangular block resting on that shelf, so every input
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:46:#      water pixel is supported and no water pixel starts with background on both horizontal sides.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:50:#      2. the output is a compact crop showing only the lower basin rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:54:#    - The picture is split into two bands: source shelf high above, basin comb low below. That keeps
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:56:#    - Basin walls stay rectilinear and adjacent, so even overflow cases look like one coherent basin
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:60:#      one must identify the basin region after simulating on the large board and return only that
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/39/code.py:63:#      the size increase and the basin-only crop are both learnable from a few demonstrations.
